Assembled from official Termux `.deb` packages (packages.termux.dev) by
`tool/fetch_android_runtime.sh`. The native closure shipped in
`python-runtime.bin` (versions move between rebuilds — re-derive with
`tar -tzf assets/bin/android/<abi>/python-runtime.bin`) includes, alongside
CPython itself:

| Library | License |
| ------- | ------- |
| OpenSSL 3 (libssl/libcrypto) | Apache-2.0 with the OpenSSL/SSLeay exception |
| libsqlite3, libreadline, libhistory, libgdbm(_compat) | Public domain (SQLite); GPL-3.0-or-later (Readline/gdbm) |
| ncurses family (libncurses, libtinfo, libtermcap, libpanel*, libmenu*, libform*, libcurses) | X11-style permissive |
| zlib (libz), zstd (libzstd), brotli (python pkg) | zlib license; BSD-3-Clause; MIT |
| liblzma, libbz2, libffi, libexpat, libcrypt (libxcrypt) | Public domain (XZ Utils); bzip2 license; MIT; MIT-style (Expat); LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| libandroid-support, libandroid-posix-semaphore | ISC |

**python-yt-dlp 2026.08.19** — The Unlicense.
From the Termux `python-yt-dlp` package; not the PyInstaller build.
Upstream's own note: standalone zipimport executables additionally carry
GPLv3+ code, and the project as a whole is Unlicense.

**brotli 1.2.0** — MIT.
**pycryptodomex 3.23.0** — BSD-2-Clause / Public Domain.

**ffmpeg + ffprobe (static, minimal)** — LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Built by `tool/fetch_ffmpeg_android.sh` with `--enable-small`, no external
codec libraries and no `--enable-gpl` / `--enable-nonfree`; only the file/pipe
protocols, the mp4/matroska/webm demuxers and muxers, H.264/HEVC/VP9/AAC/Opus
parsers and the matching bitstream filters. The build is byte-for-byte from
upstream ffmpeg 8.1.3 source; rebuilding it is subject to ffmpeg's upstream
license only, not to any copyleft obligation towards this repository.

**yt-dlp-ejs** — *not bundled.* Downloaded at runtime from PyPI when the user
enables the JavaScript-runtime integration, verified against the SHA-256 that
PyPI publishes *before* anything is unpacked (see `lib/services/ytdlp/ejs_installer.dart`).
The wheel carries ISC (`meriyah`) and MIT (`astring`) code.

2. Bundled components — Linux / Windows / macOS bundles
------------------------------------------------------

**Flutter (framework, engine, `flutter_localizations`, Dart SDK)** —
BSD-3-Clause.

No `yt-dlp` or `ffmpeg` binary is committed to this repository. Desktop builds
prefer a system install on `PATH` and otherwise download the official
single-file `yt-dlp` build at first run (`tool/fetch_binaries.sh` for the
development convenience copies, which are gitignored). Those upstream
PyInstaller builds are GPL-3.0-or-later combined works; they are fetched,
never vendored.

